WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.428 --> 00:00:06.095
(hip hop music)

00:00:12.784 --> 00:00:16.279
- I wanted to ask you
what advice you maybe have

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:18.443
for entrepreneurs that are
just about a year and a half

00:00:18.443 --> 00:00:20.501
into their journey, but I
feel like everything you

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.669
just said is perfect, just
believing in yourself,

00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:26.671
having faith, just grinding
out, doing the work,

00:00:26.671 --> 00:00:28.788
and eventually success will come.

00:00:28.788 --> 00:00:30.651
Is there anything else
that you want to add?

00:00:30.651 --> 00:00:33.087
- Yeah I wouldn't, like I
would stop comparing yourself,

00:00:33.087 --> 00:00:35.416
like who cares if you're
a year and a half in.

00:00:35.416 --> 00:00:37.001
Maybe you're 10 years in, you know?

00:00:37.001 --> 00:00:39.357
Like just, if you like what you're doing,

00:00:39.357 --> 00:00:41.194
you have a passion for
it, you have to find

00:00:41.194 --> 00:00:42.441
a way to keep going.

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:43.274
- [Victor] Absolutely.

00:00:43.274 --> 00:00:45.938
- And what I'm looking,
so like I'll look up

00:00:45.938 --> 00:00:47.708
to people right, lik I'm
not the greatest speaker

00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:50.147
in the world, you know, I love Les Brown.

00:00:50.147 --> 00:00:51.349
Either of you guys know Les Brown?

00:00:51.349 --> 00:00:52.731
- I know who Les Brown is.

00:00:52.731 --> 00:00:53.564
- [Victor] Yes.

00:00:53.564 --> 00:00:57.134
- Like young Les Brown,
that guy is sick man.

00:00:57.134 --> 00:00:58.182
- [Neil] He's like the...

00:00:58.182 --> 00:00:59.279
- I want to be young Les Brown.

00:00:59.279 --> 00:01:00.210
(group laughs)

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.202
Stuff like Young Les Brown
speaking videos, it's crazy.

00:01:04.202 --> 00:01:07.249
I'm nowhere close to young
Les Brown, but I'm not like,

00:01:07.249 --> 00:01:09.316
so what like, so what that I'm not close,

00:01:09.316 --> 00:01:10.881
like it's an aspiration to me.

00:01:10.881 --> 00:01:12.970
Like people chase perfection,
and they get pissed

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.650
when they don't hit their goal.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:15.894
It's not about the goal, it's about

00:01:15.894 --> 00:01:17.327
doing the work to get better.

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:20.283
And I think just continually,
like hard work is just,

00:01:20.283 --> 00:01:22.067
I guess in me.

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.656
When I talked about my agent.

00:01:23.656 --> 00:01:27.062
When I joined the agency, I was
the worst one at the agency.

00:01:27.062 --> 00:01:30.195
Like my agent Steve
was like you know what,

00:01:30.195 --> 00:01:31.741
I don't know if I want to take you on man.

00:01:31.741 --> 00:01:34.038
I don't know if I want
you as a client like.

00:01:34.038 --> 00:01:37.107
Everybody else who had been
with him, they were more

00:01:37.107 --> 00:01:40.845
polished speakers than
I was, and I understand.

00:01:40.845 --> 00:01:43.212
I look back at my videos like
I actually really sucked.

00:01:43.212 --> 00:01:47.463
I thought I was hot stuff,
but I really sucked.

00:01:47.463 --> 00:01:49.555
And then, he said, but you
know okay we'll take a flier,

00:01:49.555 --> 00:01:54.110
like you're our flier for the
year, we'll see what happens.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.691
And then, I just worked
harder than everybody else.

00:01:56.691 --> 00:01:58.611
When they were having a
hard time, like he asked

00:01:58.611 --> 00:01:59.444
me to do my story.

00:01:59.444 --> 00:02:01.423
One of the first
exercises, make your story.

00:02:01.423 --> 00:02:03.201
So I would make a video about my story

00:02:03.201 --> 00:02:04.781
like 15 minute video.

00:02:04.781 --> 00:02:06.894
He would review it, I'd
make it in the morning,

00:02:06.894 --> 00:02:08.470
he would review it, give me feedback.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:11.534
Afternoon I'd do it
again, another 15 minutes,

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:13.266
right he'd review it,
he'd give me feedback,

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:16.048
and do it again at night
like, three, four times a day,

00:02:16.048 --> 00:02:17.037
if he's making it.

00:02:17.037 --> 00:02:19.352
I did that intro story 40 times for him.

00:02:19.352 --> 00:02:20.185
- [Neil] Wow.

00:02:20.185 --> 00:02:21.613
- And he gave me feedback.

00:02:21.613 --> 00:02:24.773
I would make videos every
day when the other people

00:02:24.773 --> 00:02:27.523
at the agency complained
about not having time

00:02:27.523 --> 00:02:29.362
during the week to make one video.

00:02:29.362 --> 00:02:30.195
- Absolutely.

00:02:30.195 --> 00:02:33.267
- And so, I, within a
couple months, I became the

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.273
best-practiced example.

00:02:35.273 --> 00:02:38.502
They're like you guys should
be doing what Evan's doing.

00:02:38.502 --> 00:02:39.599
I was the worst one!

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:41.418
(group laughs)

00:02:41.418 --> 00:02:42.251
I was the worst!

00:02:42.251 --> 00:02:43.530
I had no talent, no skill.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.295
I just listened to their advice,
and grinded, and I became

00:02:47.295 --> 00:02:48.297
the best-practiced.

00:02:48.297 --> 00:02:49.614
So it's like, it's not for me to say

00:02:49.614 --> 00:02:50.958
I'm a genius or I'm special.

00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:52.561
Like it's the opposite, I'm not special.

00:02:52.561 --> 00:02:56.772
I'm super ordinary, introverted,
don't have the skills,

00:02:56.772 --> 00:02:58.116
and I just worked hard.

00:02:58.116 --> 00:03:01.159
I've done 4,000 videos
on my YouTube channel.

00:03:01.159 --> 00:03:03.185
Some of them are, are unlisted,

00:03:03.185 --> 00:03:04.018
they're like practice videos.

00:03:04.018 --> 00:03:06.263
There're like 4,000, you better get better

00:03:06.263 --> 00:03:08.547
if you take 4,000 shots, right?

00:03:08.547 --> 00:03:11.493
Like you have to be a new
level of garbage to not improve

00:03:11.493 --> 00:03:14.476
after trying something 4,000 times, right?

00:03:14.476 --> 00:03:16.902
So, I think people put too
much pressure on themselves

00:03:16.902 --> 00:03:18.687
to be good at the start.

00:03:18.687 --> 00:03:21.516
You see, maybe you see a
Gary V, or you see somebody

00:03:21.516 --> 00:03:23.673
like crushing it hard, and
you go out and try to do it,

00:03:23.673 --> 00:03:26.435
and your thing sucks like,
you suck at the start.

00:03:26.435 --> 00:03:28.663
And the hard part is, you have taste,

00:03:28.663 --> 00:03:29.866
but you don't have the skill.

00:03:29.866 --> 00:03:31.690
Like you know what's good.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.165
You know what a good jump shot looks like,

00:03:34.165 --> 00:03:36.664
but you can't do it, and
so when you get out there

00:03:36.664 --> 00:03:39.232
and you know that you suck, you quit.

00:03:39.232 --> 00:03:42.063
And so whatever you're making,
you know what will look good.

00:03:42.063 --> 00:03:44.296
You have certain standards
for quality, and then when

00:03:44.296 --> 00:03:47.115
you can't go out and make
that immediately, you quit.

00:03:47.115 --> 00:03:49.807
And so, it's good to have those standards.

00:03:49.807 --> 00:03:52.993
It's good to have like
the MJ jump shot as the

00:03:52.993 --> 00:03:56.193
thing to aspire to, but
understand that you're

00:03:56.193 --> 00:03:57.892
going to suck, you're going to fall.

00:03:57.892 --> 00:03:59.858
You're not going to get
anything the first time,

00:03:59.858 --> 00:04:01.920
and just make everything
better, everything better.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.696
Like, maybe you guys look
at your show and like,

00:04:03.696 --> 00:04:05.666
hey we love The Breakfast Club, you know.

00:04:05.666 --> 00:04:06.594
(both laugh)

00:04:06.594 --> 00:04:08.653
One of you is going to be
Charlamagne and one you know like.

00:04:08.653 --> 00:04:11.337
- Oh, goodness gracious.

00:04:11.337 --> 00:04:13.095
- It's a good show man,
like I was there at...

00:04:13.095 --> 00:04:16.262
- I feel like Charlamagne
is my spirit animal, Evan.

00:04:16.262 --> 00:04:17.901
I'm not going to lie.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:20.175
- Right so like, okay, it's
a good show to model right.

00:04:20.175 --> 00:04:22.416
So Breakfast Club awesome,
have guests come in, great.

00:04:22.416 --> 00:04:26.339
But, it takes time to be that good, right.

00:04:26.339 --> 00:04:29.125
They put a ton of practice
in, and so, it's like

00:04:29.125 --> 00:04:31.399
that's the ideal, and here's
where we are and just,

00:04:31.399 --> 00:04:33.375
every show needs to be
better like, whoever you

00:04:33.375 --> 00:04:35.229
bring on next, that show has to be better

00:04:35.229 --> 00:04:37.189
than that Evan Carmichael show.

00:04:37.189 --> 00:04:39.273
Let's see it, and you just
keep building your way up,

00:04:39.273 --> 00:04:41.627
and you get to be at a higher level so,

00:04:41.627 --> 00:04:44.399
I think it's hard when people
see that they don't have,

00:04:44.399 --> 00:04:46.238
they know what looks good
and they can't do it,

00:04:46.238 --> 00:04:47.898
and they just quit too soon.

00:04:47.898 --> 00:04:49.100
Thank you guys so much for watching.

